<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solve simultaneous equations graphically (curve and line)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Solve the following simultaneous equations graphically</strong>, for \( {@xlo@} \le x \le {@xhi@} \).</p>
\[ {#eq1tex#} \qquad \text{and} \qquad {#eq2tex#} \]
<p><strong>(a)</strong> Plot both graphs on the grid. Drag the <span style="color:#c62828"><strong>red point</strong></span> to place the curve \( {#eq1tex#} \), and drag the two <span style="color:#1565c0"><strong>blue points</strong></span> (at different positions) to place the straight line \( {#eq2tex#} \). The points snap to the grid.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans1="refV" input-ref-ans2="refP" input-ref-ans3="refQ" width="640px" height="560px"]]
var xlo = {#xlo#}, xhi = {#xhi#}, ymin = {#ymin#}, ymax = {#ymax#};
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [xlo - 0.8, ymax + 1.2, xhi + 0.8, ymin - 1.2],
    axis: false, grid: false, keepaspectratio: false,
    showCopyright: false, showNavigation: false,
    pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});
/* labelled square grid, one line per whole number (explicit lines: identical in every JSXGraph version) */
var gi;
for (gi = xlo - 1; gi != xhi + 2; gi++) {
    board.create('line', [ [gi, 0], [gi, 1] ], {strokeColor: '#d4d4d4', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false, layer: 0});
}
for (gi = ymin - 2; gi != ymax + 3; gi++) {
    board.create('line', [ [0, gi], [1, gi] ], {strokeColor: '#d4d4d4', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false, layer: 0});
}
board.create('axis', [ [0,0], [1,0] ], {strokeColor: '#222222', strokeWidth: 2,
    ticks: {ticksDistance: 1, insertTicks: false, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10}});
board.create('axis', [ [0,0], [0,1] ], {strokeColor: '#222222', strokeWidth: 2,
    ticks: {ticksDistance: 1, insertTicks: false, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10}});
board.create('text', [xhi + 0.7, 0.5, 'x'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'right', fontSize: 16});
board.create('text', [0.3, ymax + 1.1, 'y'], {fixed: true, anchorY: 'top', fontSize: 16});
board.create('text', [-0.12, -0.1, '0'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'right', anchorY: 'top', fontSize: 12});

/* free handles, snapped to the grid.  Start positions are never a correct answer. */
var V  = board.create('point', [1, 1],  {name: '', size: 6, snapToGrid: true, snapSizeX: 1, snapSizeY: 1,
    strokeColor: '#c62828', fillColor: '#c62828', showInfobox: true});
var P1 = board.create('point', [0, -1], {name: '', size: 6, snapToGrid: true, snapSizeX: 1, snapSizeY: 1,
    strokeColor: '#1565c0', fillColor: '#1565c0', showInfobox: true});
var P2 = board.create('point', [2, -1], {name: '', size: 6, snapToGrid: true, snapSizeX: 1, snapSizeY: 1,
    strokeColor: '#1565c0', fillColor: '#1565c0', showInfobox: true});

/* the curve y = x^2 moved so that its turning point is V; the line through P1 and P2 */
var curve = board.create('functiongraph', [function(t) { return (t - V.X()) * (t - V.X()) + V.Y(); }, xlo, xhi],
    {strokeColor: '#c62828', strokeWidth: 3});
var line = board.create('line', [P1, P2], {strokeColor: '#1565c0', strokeWidth: 3});

stack_jxg.bind_point(refV, V);
stack_jxg.bind_point(refP, P1);
stack_jxg.bind_point(refQ, P2);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<div style="display:none">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Use your graph to write down the solutions of the simultaneous equations. Give each solution as a point \( [x, y] \) with whole-number values. You may enter the two solutions in either order.</p>
<div>Solution 1: [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</div>
<div>Solution 2: [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a) Plotting the graphs.</strong></p>
<p>The <span style="color:#c62828"><strong>curve</strong></span> \( {#eq1tex#} \) is the graph of \( y=x^2 \) moved vertically, so its turning point is \( (0,\ {@-bb@}) \). A table of values gives more points to join with a smooth curve:</p>
\[ \begin{array}{c|ccccc} x & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\ \hline y & {@cvals[1]@} & {@cvals[2]@} & {@cvals[3]@} & {@cvals[4]@} & {@cvals[5]@} \end{array} \]
<p>The <span style="color:#1565c0"><strong>straight line</strong></span> \( {#eq2tex#} \) needs only two points (a third is a good check):</p>
\[ \begin{array}{c|ccc} x & 0 & 1 & 2 \\ \hline y & {@lvals[1]@} & {@lvals[2]@} & {@lvals[3]@} \end{array} \]
[[jsxgraph width="640px" height="560px"]]
var xlo = {#xlo#}, xhi = {#xhi#}, ymin = {#ymin#}, ymax = {#ymax#};
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [xlo - 0.8, ymax + 1.2, xhi + 0.8, ymin - 1.2],
    axis: false, grid: false, keepaspectratio: false,
    showCopyright: false, showNavigation: false,
    pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});
/* labelled square grid, one line per whole number (explicit lines: identical in every JSXGraph version) */
var gi;
for (gi = xlo - 1; gi != xhi + 2; gi++) {
    board.create('line', [ [gi, 0], [gi, 1] ], {strokeColor: '#d4d4d4', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false, layer: 0});
}
for (gi = ymin - 2; gi != ymax + 3; gi++) {
    board.create('line', [ [0, gi], [1, gi] ], {strokeColor: '#d4d4d4', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false, layer: 0});
}
board.create('axis', [ [0,0], [1,0] ], {strokeColor: '#222222', strokeWidth: 2,
    ticks: {ticksDistance: 1, insertTicks: false, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10}});
board.create('axis', [ [0,0], [0,1] ], {strokeColor: '#222222', strokeWidth: 2,
    ticks: {ticksDistance: 1, insertTicks: false, minorTicks: 0, majorHeight: 10}});
board.create('text', [xhi + 0.7, 0.5, 'x'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'right', fontSize: 16});
board.create('text', [0.3, ymax + 1.1, 'y'], {fixed: true, anchorY: 'top', fontSize: 16});
board.create('text', [-0.12, -0.1, '0'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'right', anchorY: 'top', fontSize: 12});

var bb = {#bb#}, aa = {#aa#};
var curve = board.create('functiongraph', [function(t) { return t * t - bb; }, xlo, xhi],
    {strokeColor: '#c62828', strokeWidth: 3, fixed: true});
var L1 = board.create('point', [0, bb],      {visible: false, withLabel: false, name: ''});
var L2 = board.create('point', [1, aa + bb], {visible: false, withLabel: false, name: ''});
var line = board.create('line', [L1, L2], {strokeColor: '#1565c0', strokeWidth: 3, fixed: true});

/* label placement: try 24 directions, keep the one whose label box stays furthest from the curve, the line,
   both axes and the board edges (distances measured in screen pixels) */
function labelAttr(px, py) {
    var ux = board.unitX, uy = board.unitY, R = 44;
    function clear(x, y) {
        var dCurve = Math.abs(y - (x * x - bb)) * uy / Math.sqrt(1 + Math.pow(2 * x * uy / ux, 2));
        var dLine = Math.abs(y - aa * x - bb) * uy / Math.sqrt(1 + Math.pow(aa * uy / ux, 2));
        return Math.min(dCurve, dLine, Math.abs(x) * ux, Math.abs(y) * uy,
            (x - (xlo - 0.8)) * ux, (xhi + 0.8 - x) * ux, (ymax + 1.2 - y) * uy, (y - (ymin - 1.2)) * uy);
    }
    var cands = [], score = [], k;
    for (k = 0; k != 24; k++) { cands.push(k * Math.PI / 12); }
    score = cands.map(function(t) {
        var cx = px + R * Math.cos(t) / ux, cy = py + R * Math.sin(t) / uy;
        return Math.min(clear(cx, cy), clear(cx - 36 / ux, cy), clear(cx + 36 / ux, cy));
    });
    var t = cands[score.indexOf(Math.max.apply(null, score))];
    return {offset: [Math.round(R * Math.cos(t)), Math.round(R * Math.sin(t))], anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle'};
}
var sols = [ [{#sx1#}, {#sy1#}], [{#sx2#}, {#sy2#}] ];
sols.forEach(function(sp) {
    board.create('segment', [ [sp[0], sp[1]], [sp[0], 0] ], {dash: 2, strokeColor: '#777777', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false});
    board.create('segment', [ [sp[0], sp[1]], [0, sp[1]] ], {dash: 2, strokeColor: '#777777', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false});
    var lab = labelAttr(sp[0], sp[1]);
    lab.fontSize = 15;
    board.create('point', sp, {name: '(' + sp[0] + ', ' + sp[1] + ')', size: 5,
        strokeColor: '#2e7d32', fillColor: '#2e7d32', fixed: true, label: lab});
});
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p><strong>(b) Reading the solutions from the graph.</strong> The line and the curve cross at the two green points. The dashed guides show their coordinates:</p>
\[ [{@sx1@},\ {@sy1@}] \qquad \text{and} \qquad [{@sx2@},\ {@sy2@}]. \]
<p><strong>Why these are solutions.</strong> A solution of simultaneous equations must make <em>both</em> equations true at the same time. Substitute each point back into the two equations.</p>
<p>For \( x={@sx1@},\ y={@sy1@} \):</p>
\[ \begin{align*}
\text{Curve: } x^2-(b) &= ({@sx1@})^2-({@bb@}) = {@sy1@} = y \; \checkmark \\
\text{Line: } a\cdot x+(b) &= ({@aa@})\cdot({@sx1@})+({@bb@}) = {@sy1@} = y \; \checkmark
\end{align*} \]
<p>For \( x={@sx2@},\ y={@sy2@} \):</p>
\[ \begin{align*}
\text{Curve: } x^2-(b) &= ({@sx2@})^2-({@bb@}) = {@sy2@} = y \; \checkmark \\
\text{Line: } a\cdot x+(b) &= ({@aa@})\cdot({@sx2@})+({@bb@}) = {@sy2@} = y \; \checkmark
\end{align*} \]
<p>Each point gives the same value of \( y \) in both equations, so the line and the curve really do meet there: the solutions are \( x={@sx1@},\ y={@sy1@} \) and \( x={@sx2@},\ y={@sy2@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
